        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The pocket door is the better door and the bigger job. It closes against a jamb, takes a privacy lock and leaves the floor and the wall clear, which makes it the right choice for bathrooms, bedrooms and offices in new construction, or wherever the wall is being opened anyway.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The barn door is the practical retrofit. It goes up on finished walls without demolition, costs far less in an existing house, and is excellent on pantries, closets, laundries and openings where sealing does not matter. Check what is inside the wall before deciding, because that usually decides for you.
          </p>
